  "steps": [
    "Loaded 1,000 loan applications (UCI Statlog German Credit) and decoded the A11/A12\u2026 attribute codes into readable categories.",
    "Kept 13 features a loan officer would enter; left out sex / marital status and foreign-worker status.",
    "Built one scikit-learn Pipeline: scaling for numbers, one-hot encoding for categories.",
    "Compared Logistic Regression, a tuned SVC (grid search inside each fold), Random Forest and Gradient Boosting with stratified 5-fold cross-validation.",
    "Picked Random Forest by ROC-AUC, then chose the decision threshold that minimises expected cost (bad loan = 5\u00d7 a rejected good one) on out-of-fold predictions.",
    "Evaluated once on a held-out 20% test set and exported the pipeline to ONNX for the browser."
  ],
  "dataset": {
    "name": "Statlog (German Credit Data), UCI",
    "url": "https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/144/statlog+german+credit+data",
    "rows": 1000
